formation='A caller proposes through RawNode/Node. The leader assigns term/index, appends unstable entries and replicates with predecessor identity. Followers require matching predecessor, refuse committed conflicts, and queue append replies after persistence. The leader self-acks after its persistence completion and aggregates peer Match using active voter majority (both halves for joint configuration); only a quorum index in its current term directly advances commitment. Append messages and Match-capped heartbeats propagate commitment. Ready exposes committed work; the caller applies entries in order and applies configuration entries. Advance or async application replies account for completion. Rejections probe backward, heartbeats reopen flow control, and compacted history uses snapshots.'
context='A promotable node with no unapplied committed configuration changes campaigns, optionally with pre-vote. Votes require eligible vote state and an up-to-date candidate log; configured voter quorums determine election. Term dispatch rejects stale replies and usually steps down on higher terms, with pre-vote/lease exceptions. Reset clears vote aggregation, replication progress, read-only heartbeat support and transfer state while preserving the committed prefix. Storage replies are term-scoped for entry stabilization, but committed snapshot/application completion survives term changes. Transfer suppresses proposals until success, abort or timeout. Applied configuration changes alter voter eligibility; snapshots/restart restore membership and history.'
connection='The term and active configuration jointly qualify support: a leader consumes only current-context responses from tracked participants, while quorum evaluation selects voters and joint majorities. Membership application can reinterpret existing Match and advance commitment without a new reply. A new leader resets remote Match, appends a new-term empty entry, and cannot campaign past known unapplied configuration changes. Pending read heartbeat support is reset, but the separate pre-commit read queue survives reset. Applying a joint configuration sets AutoLeave; application completion may propose its exit, while concurrent transfer may reject that proposal. Established decisions remain a prefix through authority changes; persistence and application completion have distinct response rules.'
mapdoc=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured Go raft module: Node/RawNode state machine, quorum/tracker/configuration and in-memory storage support; caller supplies durable storage, transport, regular ticks and application execution.',protocol_contexts=['Raft instance identity, term, role, log prefix and active membership'],external_interfaces=['Node','RawNode','Storage','Ready and local storage messages'],ownership=['Node goroutine serializes state; RawNode requires caller serialization.','Caller owns durable writes, transport and state-machine application.'],source_ids=['s_raw_init','s_node_loop','s_usage','s_storage_contract']),activities=acts,behaviors=B,facts=F,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='raft.appliedTo / abortLeaderTransfer',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b_application','b_transfer'],reason='Automatic exit rejected during transfer may require a later application event; identify whether caller duties or an internal retry guarantees that event.',source_ids=['s_applied','s_abort','s_ticks_roles','s_joint_contract'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='raft.switchToConfig / releasePendingReadIndexMessages',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b_membership','b_reads'],reason='Commit can advance here without releasing the separate pre-commit read queue. Determine whether a legal delayed configuration application exposes this and what caller retry contract implies.',source_ids=['s_config','s_read_queue_release','s_node_contract']),dict(entry_point='Node.Ready and RawNode.ApplyConfChange documentation',disposition='deferred',reason='doc.go instructs calling ApplyConfChange for cancelled changes using NodeID zero, while Node/RawNode comments allow rejection without a call; distinguish cancellation representation and supported histories before testing.',source_ids=['s_usage','s_node_contract','s_raw_init'])],core_overview=dict(status='usable',formation=dict(explanation=formation,behavior_ids=['b_formation','b_persistence','b_application','b_recovery'],fact_ids=['f_commit'],source_ids=['s_send','s_replication_send','s_ack','s_log_matching','s_apply_completion']),context=dict(explanation=context,behavior_ids=['b_authority','b_transfer','b_membership','b_recovery'],fact_ids=['f_joint'],source_ids=['s_ticks_roles','s_campaign','s_dispatch','s_config','s_recovery']),connection=dict(explanation=connection,behavior_ids=[x['id'] for x in B],fact_ids=['f_commit','f_joint'],source_ids=['s_reset_append','s_campaign','s_config','s_applied','s_append_completion','s_read_queue_release']),open_details=['Automatic exit continuation after rejected proposal and failed transfer.','Read queue behavior when configuration application causes the first current-term commit.','Detailed snapshot/application overlap and optional lease-read assumptions.'],core_gaps=[],rationale='Representative formation and authority paths are traced through their persistence, membership, recovery and consumption boundaries. This is a usable initial map, not a claim of exhaustive correctness.'))
