question=dict(question='When applying an implicit joint configuration triggers an automatic exit proposal during an in-progress leader transfer, what implementation-owned continuation retries the exit after the transfer aborts if there is no additional application work?',importance='A missed continuation could retain the old voter quorum and prevent later reconfiguration despite the implicit transition assigning exit to Raft. This is a potential progress consequence, not an observed safety violation.',source_ids=['s_applied','s_abort','s_ticks_roles','s_proposal_read','s_joint_contract','s_conf_contract'],participants=['Current leader','Transfer target','Voters in incoming and outgoing configurations','Caller apply/transport loop'],objects=['AutoLeave joint configuration','pendingConfIndex','leadTransferee','Applied-index completion'],contexts=['Implicit joint change already committed','Leader transfer overlaps application completion','Transfer later fails or aborts while leader remains in office'],event_paths=['Commit and apply implicit joint change -> application completion calls appliedTo -> Step rejects auto-exit proposal during transfer -> transfer aborts -> inspect enabled continuations'],activity_classes=['A4','A1','A2'],behavior_ids=['b_membership','b_application','b_transfer'],fact_ids=['f_joint'],supporting_behavior_ids={'b_formation':'Establishes the committed configuration entry and subsequent proposal admission under the current leader.','b_persistence':'Determines when local append and apply completion events can legally overlap transfer.','b_authority':'Successful transfer/new election supplies a fresh-term entry; it is counterevidence and a different continuation from a failed transfer.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['appliedTo retries on each subsequent applied entry; a successful new leader appends an empty entry.','Empty exit proposals cannot be refused by size accounting.','Normal proposals can be dropped and require caller retry; implicit exit ownership must be distinguished from generic proposal semantics.'],unknowns=['Whether the documented implicit exit responsibility requires retry without further client proposals after a failed transfer.','Whether a legal producer history can leave no pending application work when the transfer aborts.','Whether timers, duplicate responses, configuration events or other internal paths retry independently of a later applied entry.'],trigger_rationale='The implicit-transition API assigns exit to Raft. appliedTo explicitly admits transfer rejection and relies on a next advance, while abortLeaderTransfer only clears a field. Inspect all callers and pending-work production before choosing a controlled execution; this is more discriminating than testing already composed durability guards or the ReadIndex path whose caller retry duty is explicit.',disposition='needs_specific_evidence',preferred_check='source_review',priority=2)
